{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"For an ordinary new series added to an existing trust via a Rule 485(a) post-effective amendment, the usual effectiveness period is **75 days after filing** under Rule 485(a)(2), unless the SEC accelerates effectiveness or another provision applies. It is not an end-to-end launch guarantee: the clock addresses registration-statement effectiveness, not completion of all launch work (for example, exchange listing, seed capital, operational readiness, or any required regulatory steps).\n\nA **new trust’s initial registration** is different: it generally becomes effective **no earlier than 60 days after its initial filing** under Investment Company Act § 8(a), absent acceleration."}}
